.TH "EPX\-SCHEMAS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-schemas \- read, create, change and delete custom schemas and schema references
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas [flags]
epx schemas [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads custom schemas, the attribute sets that extend Emporix entities. TYPES lists the entity types a schema applies to and ATTRIBUTES counts its top\-level attributes (\fB\-o json\fR prints their definitions). \fBepx schemas references\fR reads schema references and \fBepx schemas types\fR the entity types that have schemas.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR. Its writes require the schema.schema_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx schemas create"
Create a schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a schema from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: its name (translations), the entity types it extends and its attributes, such as \fBepx schemas parse \-o json\fR prints them once a name and types are added. It prints the id that Emporix answers with; one that exists already is a conflict. Name entity types by their ids, with _, such as VENDOR_LOCATION.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx schemas delete"
Delete a schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the schema ID, every version of it. Emporix answers an unknown ID as a deleted one (204), so epx exits with 0.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx schemas get"
Show one schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads custom schemas, the attribute sets that extend Emporix entities. TYPES lists the entity types a schema applies to and ATTRIBUTES counts its top\-level attributes (\fB\-o json\fR prints their definitions). \fBepx schemas references\fR reads schema references and \fBepx schemas types\fR the entity types that have schemas.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, TYPES, ATTRIBUTES, VERSION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx schemas list"
List schemas.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads custom schemas, the attribute sets that extend Emporix entities. TYPES lists the entity types a schema applies to and ATTRIBUTES counts its top\-level attributes (\fB\-o json\fR prints their definitions). \fBepx schemas references\fR reads schema references and \fBepx schemas types\fR the entity types that have schemas.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, TYPES, ATTRIBUTES, VERSION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx schemas parse"
Parse a JSON schema file into a schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas parse [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Parses the JSON schema file of \fB\-\-json\-schema\fR into the schema that Emporix makes of it, and stores nothing: the table lists its attributes; \fB\-o json\fR prints the schema, which \fBepx schemas create\fR takes once its missing members, such as its name and types, are added, or, with \fB\-\-id\fR, \fBepx schemas update ID\fR.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a multipart/form\-data body, which the flags make.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR
Opt in to requesting schema.schema_manage, which can also change data (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among KEY, TYPE, REQUIRED, LOCALIZED, READ ONLY.
.TP
\fB\-\-id <ID>\fR
ID of the schema that the file updates.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\-schema <PATH>\fR
JSON schema file in PATH to parse (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx schemas references"
Read, create, change and delete schema references.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas references [flags]
epx schemas references [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads schema references: schemas uploaded as a JSON schema file, for attribute types that schemas cannot define. TYPES lists the entity types a reference applies to; the file\(aqs URL is only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the schema.schema_manage scope.
.SS "epx schemas references create"
Create a schema reference.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas references create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a schema reference: the JSON schema file of \fB\-\-json\-schema\fR with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, which names the reference and the entity types it applies to, such as \fB{"name": {"en": "Specifications"}, "types": ["PRODUCT"]}\fR. It prints the id that Emporix answers with; one that exists already is a conflict. It sends both as a multipart/form\-data body, the file as its file field. Name entity types by their ids, with _, such as VENDOR_LOCATION. A read of a reference shows that type as VENDOR.LOCATION; a write that sends it so makes Emporix answer reads of references with 500.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON in PATH, sent byte for byte as the body field of the form (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\-schema <PATH>\fR
JSON schema file in PATH that the reference holds (required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx schemas references delete"
Delete a schema reference.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas references delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the schema reference ID. The JSON schema file that it holds stays where Emporix stored it. Emporix answers an unknown ID as a deleted one (204), so epx exits with 0.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx schemas references get"
Show one reference.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas references get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads schema references: schemas uploaded as a JSON schema file, for attribute types that schemas cannot define. TYPES lists the entity types a reference applies to; the file\(aqs URL is only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
