.SS "epx schemas references update"
Replace a schema reference.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas references update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the schema reference ID: the JSON schema file of \fB\-\-json\-schema\fR with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, which names the reference, its types and, as metadata.version, the version that it replaces (VERSION in \fBepx schemas references get ID\fR). An unknown ID is not found. It sends both as a multipart/form\-data body, the file as its file field. Name entity types by their ids, with _, such as VENDOR_LOCATION. A read of a reference shows that type as VENDOR.LOCATION; a write that sends it so makes Emporix answer reads of references with 500.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON in PATH, sent byte for byte as the body field of the form (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\-schema <PATH>\fR
JSON schema file in PATH that the reference holds (required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx schemas types"
List the entity types that have schemas.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas types [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the entity types that have at least one schema, such as PRODUCT or CUSTOM_ENTITY.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among TYPE.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx schemas update"
Replace a schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the schema ID with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: its name, types and attributes and, optionally, as metadata.version, the version that it replaces (VERSION in \fBepx schemas get ID\fR; an older one is a conflict). Every update, with a version or without, releases a new version of the schema. An unknown ID is not found. Name entity types by their ids, with _, such as VENDOR_LOCATION.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx schemas update\-types"
Change the entity types of a schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx schemas update\-types ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sets the entity types of the schema ID to those of the JSON array in \fB\-\-file\fR, such as \fB["PRODUCT", "ORDER"]\fR, in the version that \fB\-\-version\fR names: the latest is VERSION in \fBepx schemas get ID\fR, and an earlier one may be named too. \fB\-\-mode\fR ADD adds the types instead, REMOVE removes them. It releases no new version of the schema. An unknown ID is not found. Name entity types by their ids, with _, such as VENDOR_LOCATION.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the schema.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-\-mode <MODE>\fR
MODE in which the types given change the schema\(aqs (REPLACE without it): REPLACE, ADD or REMOVE.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-version <VERSION>\fR
VERSION of the schema whose types change, a whole number (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
